menu "Sorting Camera"

    config SORTING_CAM_FRAME_TRANSPORT
        bool "Enable TCP/UDP frame transport"
        default n
        help
            Starts the raw frame transport (TCP listener on STREAM_TRANSPORT_PORT,
            the accepted TCP client, and a UDP receive socket) in addition to the
            HTTP baseline. The baseline (status/snapshot/config on port 80, MJPEG
            on port 81, discovery on port 48888) is the only path used by the
            desktop app and the benchmark harness.

            Socket arithmetic, counting httpd's fixed 3-socket overhead per
            instance: control httpd 6+3 = 9, MJPEG httpd 2+3 = 5, discovery UDP =
            1, so the baseline already holds 15 of CONFIG_LWIP_MAX_SOCKETS=16.
            Enabling the transport adds 3 more (18 > 16) and therefore does NOT
            fit: leave this off unless a raw-transport client is being used, and
            raise CONFIG_LWIP_MAX_SOCKETS to at least 19 first.

endmenu
